    "result_text": "All 275 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS, including the new `Cp13Tests` and all existing acceptance/controller tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation cap by adding a new step to the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline that rejects the 21st owner registered for the same day with **400 Bad Request**.\n\n**New files:**\n- `function/owner/CheckDailyOwnerLimit.java` \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's registration date; throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count already \u2265 20.\n- `escalation/DailyOwnerLimitException.java` \u2014 checked exception.\n- `escalation/DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 maps it to a 400 `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing handler pattern.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DailyOwnerLimitException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `checkDailyLimit` step (under the `transaction` governance) between the duplicate-email check and membership-number assignment, so an over-cap owner is rejected before it reaches `SaveOwner`.\n\nThe check keys off the owner's registration date (defaulted to today by `BuildOwner`), matching the spec's \"created today (by registration date)\" wording, and guards against a null date so it can't NPE.",
